# ACME-2: scratch files stay local

A file named `*.scratch.*` is a draft or a note to self. It belongs on the author's machine, not in review or in the history.

Honours the rule: the note is kept outside the repository, or written up as a real document such as `docs/health-route.md`.

Breaks the rule: `packages/api/notes.scratch.md` is committed.

## Settings

`marker`, default `".scratch."`, is the part of a file name that marks a scratch file. A repository that marks only scratch notes sets:

```json
"clauseSettings": {
  "acme/ACME-2#scratch-files": { "marker": ".scratch.md" }
}
```
